WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.670
Two people chatting.

2
00:00:01.720 --> 00:00:05.050
Underneath them, a live
transcript scrolls.

3
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:06.250
Erm.

4
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:07.420
A pause.

5
00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:10.990
A sentence that starts,
stops, and starts again.

6
00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.240
Then two voices at once.

7
00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:17.130
Now the same chat, tidied
into neat written dialogue.

8
00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:19.300
Every erm has gone.

9
00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:21.830
And somehow, something's missing.

10
00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:24.410
So is all that mess a problem?

11
00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:26.830
In this mission, you'll name the features,

12
00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:29.110
from fillers to false starts.

13
00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:31.430
Do only nervous speakers use them?

14
00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:33.830
You'll see how conversation is organised,

15
00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:35.110
turn by turn.

16
00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:37.860
And you'll find turns
that come in linked pairs,

17
00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:39.850
like a question and its answer.

18
00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:43.740
Your mission: decide whether
all that mess is a problem.
